Reference implementations
================================================================================

No code from the following was copied into sushi. They were read as
specifications while writing our own implementations of the same architectures,
and they are listed because they made that work possible.

  * poolside `modeling_laguna.py` (Apache-2.0), the reference for the `laguna`
    architecture.
  * The `inkling_mlx/` package bundled with Thinking Machines' Inkling Small
    checkpoints (Apache-2.0), the reference and parity oracle for
    `inkling_mm_model`.
  * turboderp/exllamav3 (MIT), the EXL3 format. `src/exl3/` re-implements the
    16x16 trellis packing, the MCG and MUL1 decodes, the tensor-core permutation
    and the suh/svh Hadamard from that reference. `src/encoder/` re-implements
    the quantizer procedure in `modules/quant/exl3_lib/quantize.py`: block-RMS
    regularize, the 0.025 diagonal damping, 16-row block LDL, reverse LDLQ and
    the golden-section global scale folded into suh. The tile search is our own
    Viterbi over the same trellis, a CPU reference and a Metal kernel, not their
    CUDA kernel, and the output-Hessian sensitivity path is not implemented. No
    exllamav3 code is shipped.

